/-!
# Artinian boundary models for Hankel quotients

The one-element coefficient ring, the integers, integers modulo four and
the product of two copies of the integers give contrasting Artinian
behaviour for rational-normal-curve coordinate rings. The small-degree
models retain the full one-variable and two-variable polynomial quotients.
The models distinguish Artinian coefficients from Artinian Hankel quotients
and include nonzero nilpotent and orthogonal quotient elements.
-/
